one worth your attention as a general hazard:

  `downbeatColor` read `--downbeat` via `getComputedStyle().getPropertyValue()` and parsed channels
  out of it. An UNREGISTERED custom property's computed value is its literal token stream, so that
  call returns the string `oklch(78% 0.08 250)` and a digit regex turns it into `rgb(78, 0, 250)` —
  an indigo. Every test fed it `rgb()` literals, so three green tests sat on top of a feature that
  could never have worked. It now builds the oklch string itself and interpolates per channel in
  OKLCH, as `_dbColor` does. **Our shared rule "canvas colours come from getComputedStyle, never
  literal oklch" is right for flat colours and wrong for ramps** — a ramp needs channels and a token
  stream has none. Worth a line in the spec's §9.1 before M6's chroma heatmap hits the same wall.

