test should seed tokens:

| how the token was set | `getComputedStyle(el).getPropertyValue()` returns |
|---|---|
| a `<style>` block on `:root` | `oklch(90%0.012 240)` — **the space after `90%` eaten** |
| inline on the element or an ancestor | exact |
| never defined | `""` |

Two consequences beyond M4. A canvas test that seeds tokens from a stylesheet and asserts an exact
string fails for a reason that has nothing to do with the component — so seed them **inline**. And an
undefined token makes `ctx.fillStyle = ""` a **silent no-op that leaves the previous colour**, so any
`getComputedStyle` token read on a canvas wants a per-token fallback; in the app `tokens.css` is
loaded and it never fires, but a thumbnail, a failed stylesheet or a bare test render paints garbage.
**M6's chroma heatmap hits both of these**, on top of the ramp rule we already knew.

